              satisfies the requirement of the ZF axiom of collection.
          %p Thus, SEAR and SEARC are at least equiconsistent with ZF and ZFC, respectively. In fact, SEARC and ZFC are equivalent, in the sense that passage back and forth in either direction yields an equivalent model. However, passage from SEAR to ZF and back again can lose information, if there are sets in the model of SEAR which do not admit any well-founded extensional relation (this doesn’t happen in the presence of choice, since then every set can be well-ordered).
          %h3#type_theory_and_internalization Type theory and internalization
          %p
            Every topos has an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
