            %em Intuitionistic Bounded SEAR
            can be treated as a type theory and interpreted internally in any topos with a NNO. Of course, if the topos is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+topos"} boolean
          %p One can also write down stronger axioms on a topos such that if they are satisfied, then full Intuitionistic SEAR can be interpreted “internally” in that topos, extending the usual internal logic.
          %h2#making_alternate_primitive_choices Making alternate primitive choices
          %h3#threesorted_sear Three-sorted SEAR
          %p
            An alternate formulation of the theory uses three
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sorts"} sorts
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/three-sorted+set+theory"} three-sorted set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            between the sort of elements and the sort of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↬
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi:A \looparrowright B
            also becomes a ternary relation between the sort of relations, and two copies of the sort of sets. There is a quinary relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} holds
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{holds}(A, B, \varphi, a, b)
            between all three sorts, which says that given sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
            holds for element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↬
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi:A \looparrowright B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
