          %h3#eqfree Eliminating equality
          %p
            As stated SEAR includes a fundamental “equality” relation on elements of a given set. However, we can also make equality into
            = succeed "." do
              %em structure
          %p
            Consider a theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-sets"} pre-sets
            = succeed "," do
              %em elements
            %em pre-relations
            as in SEAR, with “pre-sets” replacing sets, except that there is no given equality relation on
            = succeed "." do
              %em anything
            %em definition
            of what it means for two parallel pre-relations to be equal, i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo =
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi=\psi
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(x,y)\Leftrightarrow\psi(x,y)
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            in the source and target of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
          %p
            Before stating the version of Axiom 2 we need some definitions. We define a
            %strong set
            to be a preset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence pre-relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} =_A
            which satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+substitution"} principle of substitution
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+of+indiscernibles"} identity of indiscernibles
            %strong relation
            between sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,{=_A})
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B,{=_B})
            is a pre-relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↬
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi:A\looparrowright B
            which is
            %em extensional
            in the sense that if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
